{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"16 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,29.575,3.651,3.268,"State Bank of India"],[13.889,14.731,34.852,2.373,2.124,"Record profit, with a stake sale inside"],[13.889,20.845,52.931,1.809,1.634,"State Bank of India reported a record Q2 FY27 net profit of ₹23,038 cr on 3"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"November, up 14%; the shares have gained 11% since (NIFTY: 6%). The record"],[13.889,23.733,52.936,1.809,1.634,"includes ₹7,288 cr from selling 6.3% of SBI Funds Management around its IPO;"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"a year earlier Yes Bank brought ₹4,593 cr. Before these gains, and our estimate"],[13.889,26.621,52.934,1.809,1.634,"of the tax on them, profit rose 3.5% and operating profit fell 1%. Bond yields"],[13.889,28.065,52.951,1.809,1.634,"rose, turning a ₹2,877 cr trading gain into a ₹1,277 cr loss, and costs grew 10%."],[13.889,29.509,52.931,1.809,1.634,"The lending business did well: net interest income rose 15%, loans 18%, and"],[13.889,30.954,27.369,1.809,1.634,"loan-loss provisions were 0.22% of loans."],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"1) Rising rates help: 49% of domestic loans are tied to the repo or T-bill rate and"],[13.889,34.883,52.951,1.809,1.634,"reprice faster than deposits, and the bank expects a 50 bp repo rise in December."],[13.889,36.328,52.936,1.809,1.634,"We take the margin from 2.95% in FY27E to 3.02% in FY28E; net interest"],[13.889,37.772,52.964,1.809,1.634,"income grows 16% and 15%. 2) Provisions rise from a trough. Expected-credit-"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"loss rules start on 1 April 2027: the bank estimates a ₹19,500 cr charge to"],[13.889,40.684,52.959,1.809,1.634,"reserves (₹21 a share), and we raise loan provisions to 0.42% of loans in FY28E"],[13.889,42.128,52.931,1.809,1.634,"from 0.25% in H1. 3) The wage settlement ends in October 2027; we add ₹7,800"],[13.889,43.572,52.829,1.809,1.634,"cr a year from then. EPS before one-offs grows 9%, 16% and 8% in FY27E-29E."],[13.889,46.034,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹1,130 averages two methods. A sum of parts gives"],[13.889,47.502,52.964,1.809,1.634,"₹1,145: the bank at 1.3x book (₹928), on a 12% cost of equity and a 13% long-"],[13.889,48.946,52.934,1.809,1.634,"run return on book, plus subsidiaries at market value less 20% (₹217). SBI’s"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"three-year average P/E of 9.5x gives ₹1,123. At ₹1,080 the shares assume a"],[13.889,51.834,52.951,1.809,1.634,"12.5% long-run return; the bank guides to 1% on assets, about 13% on equity."],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Consensus is ₹1,233; 34 of 40 brokers say buy. We turn positive if returns hold"],[13.889,54.722,52.936,1.809,1.634,"near 14% under the new provisioning rules (target ₹1,200). Risks: drought"],[13.889,56.167,46.242,1.809,1.634,"restructuring of up to ₹10,000 cr of farm loans; Yes Bank AT-1 ruling."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,67.265,1.489,1.022,0.915,"800"],[15.268,65.851,1.489,1.022,0.915,"900"],[14.451,64.436,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,000"],[14.451,63.022,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,100"],[14.451,61.607,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,200"],[14.451,60.195,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,300"],[18.306,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.929,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.701,67.96,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.473,67.96,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[19.25,69.131,2.019,1.275,1.111,"SBI ("],[21.272,69.157,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[21.885,69.131,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[24.969,69.131,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.279,70.291,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.536,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.292,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,70.291,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,71.356,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.359,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"11.9%"],[24.065,71.356,2.811,1.387,1.209,"12.9%